  "final_message": "Fixed: slots whose names start with an underscore (e.g. `<template #_slot2>`) are no longer dropped when the slotted component is rendered inside a conditionally-slotted parent.\n\n**Status:** reproduced, then fixed.\n\n**Reproduction.** `npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts` follows the report's structure. A `BaseLayout` has a sibling `<template v-if #randomslotname>`, and its default slot holds a `SubComponent` with `#slot1` and `#_slot2`.\n- Before the fix it exited non-zero with the reported symptom: `slot1` content rendered, `_slot2` fell back to its default content (`<div>default _slot2</div>`).\n- It passes with the sibling `v-if` template removed, so the trigger is the conditional template.\n\n**Cause.** Commit 5d166f3 changed `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` from `key !== '_'` to `!isInternalKey(key)`. `isInternalKey` matches any key starting with `_`. The conditional template makes the parent's slots dynamic, so its slot fragment bails out of optimization. The child is then mounted unoptimized, and `assignSlots` skipped every `_`-prefixed key, including the user's `_slot2`.\n\n**Fix** (all in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts`):\n- Added `isCompilerMarkerKey`, which matches only the compiler markers `_` and `__`.\n- `assignSlots` uses it instead of `isInternalKey`.\n- The stale-slot deletion in `updateSlots` uses it too. I found this second symptom while probing: a conditional `#_foo` slot never disappeared once its `v-if` turned false, because the cleanup skipped every `_`-prefixed key. It fails the same way without my change, and I fixed it here because it shares the cause.\n- `isInternalKey` is unchanged for hand-written render-function slots (`normalizeObjectSlots`), so those behave as before.\n\n**Tests added:**\n- `packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts`: the report's scenario, plus toggling a conditional `#_foo` slot off.\n- Two cases in `packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts`: `_`-prefixed slots are kept on unoptimized init, and stale `_`-prefixed dynamic slots are deleted.\n- All four new tests fail without the source change and pass with it.\n\n**Checks:** the unit suites for runtime-core, runtime-dom, vue, compiler-core, compiler-dom, server-renderer and runtime-test pass (126 files, 2352 tests). `tsc --noEmit`, eslint and prettier are clean.\n",
  "run_command": "",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts b/packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts\nindex ad87e53..abf86e9 100644\n--- a/packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts\n+++ b/packages/runtime-core/__tests__/componentSlots.spec.ts\n@@ -66,6 +66,18 @@ describe('component: slots', () => {\n     render(createBlock(Comp, null, slots), nodeOps.createElement('div'))\n   })\n \n+  test('initSlots: should keep compiled slots whose names start with an underscore (not optimized)', () => {\n+    // `h()` (as opposed to `createBlock()`) mounts without optimization, e.g.\n+    // when the component is rendered inside a BAIL fragment\n+    const _foo = () => {}\n+    const { slots } = renderWithSlots({ _foo, foo: () => {}, _: 1, __: [1] })\n+    expect(slots._foo).toBe(_foo)\n+    expect(slots).toHaveProperty('foo')\n+    // compiler markers must still not be exposed as slots\n+    expect(slots).not.toHaveProperty('_')\n+    expect(Object.keys(slots).sort()).toEqual(['_foo', 'foo'])\n+  })\n+\n   test('initSlots: should normalize object slots (when value is null, string, array)', () => {\n     const { slots } = renderWithSlots({\n       _inner: '_inner',\n@@ -162,6 +174,48 @@ describe('component: slots', () => {\n     expect(instance.slots).toHaveProperty('two')\n   })\n \n+  test('updateSlots: should delete stale dynamic slots whose names start with an underscore', async () => {\n+    const flag1 = ref(true)\n+\n+    let instance: any\n+    const Child = () => {\n+      instance = getCurrentInstance()\n+      return 'child'\n+    }\n+\n+    const Comp = {\n+      setup() {\n+        return () => [\n+          h(\n+            Child,\n+            null,\n+            createSlots({ _: 2 as any }, [\n+              flag1.value\n+                ? {\n+                    name: '_one',\n+                    fn: () => [h('span')],\n+                  }\n+                : {\n+                    name: '_two',\n+                    fn: () => [h('div')],\n+                  },\n+            ]),\n+          ),\n+        ]\n+      },\n+    }\n+    render(h(Comp), nodeOps.createElement('div'))\n+\n+    expect(instance.slots).toHaveProperty('_one')\n+    expect(instance.slots).not.toHaveProperty('_two')\n+\n+    flag1.value = false\n+    await nextTick()\n+\n+    expect(instance.slots).not.toHaveProperty('_one')\n+    expect(instance.slots).toHaveProperty('_two')\n+  })\n+\n   test('updateSlots: instance.slots should be updated correctly (when slotType is null)', async () => {\n     const flag1 = ref(true)\n \ndiff --git a/packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts b/packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts\nindex 6114f6c..5a69a86 100644\n--- a/packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts\n+++ b/packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts\n@@ -88,6 +88,11 @@ export type RawSlots = {\n \n const isInternalKey = (key: string) => key[0] === '_' || key === '$stable'\n \n+// compiler-generated markers on compiled slots objects. Unlike\n+// `isInternalKey`, this must not match user-defined slot names that happen to\n+// start with an underscore (e.g. `<template #_foo>`).\n+const isCompilerMarkerKey = (key: string) => key === '_' || key === '__'\n+\n const normalizeSlotValue = (value: unknown): VNode[] =>\n   isArray(value)\n     ? value.map(normalizeVNode)\n@@ -180,7 +185,7 @@ const assignSlots = (\n     // when rendering the optimized slots by manually written render function,\n     // do not copy the `slots._` compiler flag so that `renderSlot` creates\n     // slot Fragment with BAIL patchFlag to force full updates\n-    if (optimized || !isInternalKey(key)) {\n+    if (optimized || !isCompilerMarkerKey(key)) {\n       slots[key] = children[key]\n     }\n   }\n@@ -252,7 +257,7 @@ export const updateSlots = (\n   // delete stale slots\n   if (needDeletionCheck) {\n     for (const key in slots) {\n-      if (!isInternalKey(key) && deletionComparisonTarget[key] == null) {\n+      if (!isCompilerMarkerKey(key) && deletionComparisonTarget[key] == null) {\n         delete slots[key]\n       }\n     }\ndiff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..9ec7c34\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@\n+import { createApp, nextTick } from '../src'\n+\n+// Reproduction of the report: slot names starting with `_` are dropped when\n+// the slotted component is rendered inside a slot that bails out of\n+// optimization (a sibling conditional `<template v-if #slot>` makes the\n+// parent's slots dynamic).\n+describe('slots with names starting with an underscore', () => {\n+  it('should render slot content for `_`-prefixed names inside dynamic slots', () => {\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+\n+    const SubComponent = {\n+      template: `\n+        <slot name=\"slot1\"><div>default slot1</div></slot>\n+        <slot name=\"_slot2\"><div>default _slot2</div></slot>\n+      `,\n+    }\n+    const BaseLayout = {\n+      template: `\n+        <div>\n+          <slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot>\n+          <slot></slot>\n+        </div>\n+      `,\n+    }\n+    const App = {\n+      components: { SubComponent, BaseLayout },\n+      data: () => ({ show: true }),\n+      template: `\n+        <BaseLayout>\n+          <template v-if=\"show\" #randomslotname>\n+            <p>conditional</p>\n+          </template>\n+          <SubComponent>\n+            <template #slot1><div>slot1 content</div></template>\n+            <template #_slot2><div>_slot2 content</div></template>\n+          </SubComponent>\n+        </BaseLayout>\n+      `,\n+    }\n+    createApp(App).mount(container)\n+\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toContain('slot1 content')\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).not.toContain('default slot1')\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toContain('_slot2 content')\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).not.toContain('default _slot2')\n+  })\n+\n+  it('should remove a conditional `_`-prefixed slot when its condition turns false', async () => {\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+    const Comp = { template: `<slot name=\"_foo\"><i>default</i></slot>` }\n+    const App = {\n+      components: { Comp },\n+      data: () => ({ show: true }),\n+      template: `<Comp><template v-if=\"show\" #_foo><b>content</b></template></Comp>`,\n+    }\n+    const vm: any = createApp(App).mount(container)\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toContain('<b>content</b>')\n+\n+    vm.show = false\n+    await nextTick()\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).toContain('<i>default</i>')\n+    expect(container.innerHTML).not.toContain('content')\n+  })\n+})\n"
}
